# width: 120
# height: 40
# The git view's working-tree column at 120x40 — about 31 cells wide —
# paints every button whole. The section rows drop "Files" to keep
# `Stage All` / `Unstage All` entire, the commit row tightens its gaps
# so `Clear` fits, and a header too long for the column ends in the
# ellipsis. Before, the edge cut them to `Stage A`, `Unstage A` and
# `Clea`, with nothing to say they were cut.
shell git init -q -b main
shell git config user.email "test@mnml.dev"
shell git config user.name "mnml test"
write src/app.ts "export const name = 1;\n"
shell git add -A
shell git commit -q -m "first commit"
write src/app.ts "export const label = 1;\n"
write docs/longline.txt "a\n"
write notes.txt "b\n"
key ctrl+shift+g
wait 500
key g
expect within 3000 screen contains "3 change(s)"
expect screen contains "▾ Unstaged (3)     Stage All"
expect screen contains "▾ Staged (0)     Unstage All"
expect screen contains "  Commit   AI Message   Clear"
expect screen lacks "Stage A "
expect screen contains "WIP @ main · 3 change(s) · 2…"
